    fix(QA-DUCKBRAIN-002): per-uid pidfile dir + hermetic scratch daemons
    
    - pidfile.ts: fallback dir is now os.tmpdir()/duckbrain-<uid> (mode 0700),
      not bare os.tmpdir(). Two uids can never collide on the shared fixed-name
      pidfile; one uid's leftovers behave exactly as before.
    - pidfile.ts: accepts explicit dir override so tests can pin it.
    - helpers.ts: startDuckbrainHttp gives every scratch daemon its own
      DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR + DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH + DUCKBRAIN_CONFIG_PATH
      (temp root, empty registry schema defaults). Caller-supplied or ambient
      env values still win. cleanupDaemonDirs() reaps only dirs THIS helper made.
    - New regression suite src/cli/pidfile-isolation-qaduckbrain002.test.ts
      asserts applied pidfile location + two-daemon non-collision.
    - Existing pidfile.test.ts + unix-socket-flag.test.ts updated for the new
      per-uid fallback path.
    
    Targeted suites (pidfile + unix-socket-flag + new isolation suite): 12/12
    green. tsc --noEmit clean. Full suite verification deferred to CI (hosted
    run on this commit will confirm the wider surface).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
